# S-EPM Bidirectional Pulse Driver with FPGA Control

## Project Overview

This project explores the design of a bidirectional electrical driver and FPGA-based controller for a Switchable-polarity Electro-Permanent Magnet (S-EPM).

The system generates short, controlled current pulses through the S-EPM coil in either direction. Reversing the current direction changes the magnetic state of the device while avoiding continuous power consumption.

The project combines power-electronics hardware, circuit simulation, experimental measurements, PCB design, and FPGA-based digital control.

## System Architecture

The system is divided into two main sections:

- **Power Driver Hardware** – provides the bidirectional high-current pulse required by the S-EPM coil.
- **FPGA Controller** – generates deterministic forward and reverse pulse commands with dead-time and safety control.

The overall signal flow is:

```text
User Command
     │
     ▼
FPGA Controller
     │
     ├── Direction
     ├── Enable
     └── Pulse Timing
     │
     ▼
H-Bridge Driver
     │
     ▼
S-EPM Coil
